const threats = [
  ['Storage provider or bucket compromise', 'Blobs are AES-256-GCM ciphertext; keys are never in the bucket.'],
  ['Database or API server compromise', 'Only wrapped keys, salts, public keys and structural metadata are stored.'],
  ['The server substitutes a public key to receive a shared key', 'Keys are sealed only to users whose keys the owner certified. A new user’s keys are bound to their invite link, which the server never sees.'],
  ['The server plants a key it knows on a user', 'A shared key is used only if its certified sender signed it.'],
  ['The server moves a wrapped key or blob to another row', 'Every ciphertext authenticates the ids it belongs to.'],
  ['Someone finds the API', 'No sign-up: accounts come from the owner’s invite links. bcrypt passwords, lockout and rate limiting.'],
  ['Someone finds a new server before its owner does', 'Creating the owner needs the setup key from the server’s log or environment.'],
  ['Stolen access token', '15-minute lifetime. It grants ciphertext and short-lived URLs, not keys.'],
  ['Stolen refresh token', 'Stored hashed, rotated on every use, revoked on logout; an httpOnly cookie in browsers on the server’s own address.'],
  ['Leaked storage URL', 'Pre-signed, valid 60 seconds for downloads and 15 minutes for uploads. It yields ciphertext only.'],
  ['Passphrase guessing', 'Argon2id with a 64 MiB memory cost per guess.'],
  ['Someone learns a vault passphrase', 'It opens nothing without that account’s private keys as well.'],
  ['Someone looks at your unlocked app', 'Vaults you created are never listed; only the ones matching an entered passphrase open.'],
  ['Lost or borrowed device', 'Keys are held in memory only and destroyed on lock, after the chosen idle time (15 minutes at most), and when the app or tab closes. The exception is the app’s optional fingerprint or face unlock.'],
  ['A user should no longer have access', 'Unsharing deletes their wrapped keys and is enforced on their next request.'],
];
